f 2026-2030 FCFs @9.0%: $232 + $242 + $240 + $249 + $241 = **$1,204M**\n- Terminal value = $371M\u00d71.02 / (9.0%\u22122.0%) = **$5,406M**; PV = **$3,514M**\n- **Core EV \u2248 $4,718M** \u2014 round **$4.7B** (SBC-expensed; excludes pipeline)\n- Terminal growth 2.0% [Assumption]; terminal margin 17.6% [Assumption]\n\n### 3-5 Pipeline rNPV (Engine 4 \u2014 12% discount rate [Assumption])\n| Asset | PoS | Peak sales | Multiple | Value @launch | PV today | Basis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Alixorexton \u2014 NT1+NT2 (Ph3, BTD) | 55% | $1,200M | 4.5\u00d7 | $2,970M | $1,890M | [Assumption] \u2014 CNS base rate + Ph2 positive |\n| LUMRYZ \u2014 IH label (REVITALYZ, data [Unconfirmed] positive) | 75% | $300M | 4.0\u00d7 | $900M | $718M | [Assumption] |\n| ALKS-7290 \u2014 ADHD (Ph1; PoC Q4-26) | 12% | $1,500M | 4.0\u00d7 | $720M | $365M | [Assumption] |\n| ALKS-4510 \u2014 fatigue (Ph2a planned) | 8% | $600M | 4.0\u00d7 | $192M | $87M | [Assumption] |\n| Early platform residue | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | $50M | [Assumption] |\n| **Subtotal** | | | | | **$3,110M** | |\n| Correlation haircut (all orexin-linked) \u221210% | | | | | **\u2212$310M** | [Assumption] |\n| **Pipeline EV** | | | | | **$2,800M** | |\n\n### 3-6 Total Enterprise \u2192 Equity\n- Total EV = $4,718M + $2,800M = **$7,518M**\n- Net debt = $1,525M term loans \u2212 ~$538M cash+investments \u2248 **$987M** \u2192 use **$950M** [Estimate]\n- Equity value = **$6,568M**\n- Per share (167.76M): **$39.2** \u2014 use **$38.6** after 1.5% dilution allowance for option/SBC creep [Assumption]\n- **IV base = $38.6/share | 50% CI $32\u201348 | 80% CI $24\u201363**\n\n### 3-X Tornado (Top-3 variables become Thesis KPIs)\n1. **Alixorexton PoS/peak** ($1.2B/55% base): \u00b1$1.9B EV \u2192 **\u00b1$11/share**\n2. **VIVITROL generic timing** (2027 base vs 2029 stall): \u00b1$0.6B \u2192 **\u00b1$3.6/share**\n3. **Terminal EBIT margin** (17.6% vs 14-20%): \u00b1$1.0B \u2192 **\u00b1$6/share**\n4. WACC \u00b1100bp: \u2213$1.1B \u2192 **\u2213$6.5/share**\n\n### Reverse DCF Check\nCurrent EV $9.14B \u2212 pipeline $2.8B = implied core EV $6.34B \u2192 requires terminal growth **~4.0%** (vs our 2.0%) or a materially higher margin path. The market is not pricing our base case.\n\n### Multiples Cross-Check\n- EV / 2026E adj. EBITDA: $9.14B / $0.375B = **24.4\u00d7** \u2014 rich vs specialty-pharma 12-15\u00d7\n- 2028E normalized P/E: $48.83 / $1.14 \u2248 **43\u00d7** \u2014 prices >3 years of execution\n- P/B 4.66\u00d7 vs ROE ~4% trailing \u2014 rich\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n- **Competitive response**: Jazz (Xywav) and generics will contest LUMRYZ via contracting; J&J/Otsuka/Lundbeck contest LAI market. If alixorexton succeeds, big pharma (Lilly already validated orexin) will compete aggressively \u2014 limit the \"platform premium.\" Impact: **-2**.\n- **Reflexivity**: Rising stock enables cheap buyback (already used at $28) and strong SBC-based talent retention; a falling stock (bear case) would make the $1.5B debt feel heavier and could trigger short pressure. **Positive loop is real but currently exhausted at $48.83.**\n- **Customer evolution**: LUMRYZ moving from early adopters to mainstream narcolepsy; gross-to-net will deteriorate as payer mix broadens (LYBALVI GTN already rising to mid-30s% [Actual-Q1 call]). **Headwind.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\n### 4-1/4-2 Scenario Set\n| Scenario | Prob. | Description | 3-Yr Price (2029E) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 25% | Alixorexton Ph3 fails; VIVITROL generic 2027 with 40% erosion; LUMRYZ IH fails/plateaus | **$22** |\n| Base | 50% | Core per DCF; alixorexton 55% PoS partially reflected; LUMRYZ $600M+; LYBALVI $560M | **$50** |\n| Bull | 25% | Alixorexton positive in NT1+NT2 and IH; LUMRYZ franchise $1B; VIVITROL holds to 2031 | **$67** |\n\n**Expected 3-yr price = 0.25\u00d722 + 0.50\u00d750 + 0.25\u00d767 = $47.25** (vs T0 $48.83)\n\n### 4-3 Bayesian Update\n- Prior (CNS Ph3 base rate): 45-50%\n- Evidence: Phase-2 Vibrance-2 positive, Breakthrough Therapy designation (NT1), best-in-class oral claim \u2192 likelihood ratio \u2248 1.2\n- **Posterior PoS \u2248 55%** \u2713 (no >1.5\u00d7 breach)\n\n### 4-4/4-5 Expected Value & MoS\n- PV of expected 3-yr price @9%: $47.25 / 1.295 = **$36.5** (consistent with IV $38.6)\n- **MoS = ($38.6 \u2212 $48.83) / $38.6 = \u221226.8% \u2192 \"None\"**\n- 50% CI: $32\u201348; 80% CI: $24\u201363 [Assumption]\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\n- Market-implied horizon: at 24\u00d7 EBITDA and 43\u00d7 2028E EPS, the market capitalizes success out to 2030+ (alixorexton launch + ramp).\n- Our horizon: 3-5 years.\n- **No positive horizon arbitrage exists at $48.83**: we would be asked to pay for 2029-2030 optionality today without a margin of safety. Favorable arbitrage appears only if the market de-rates to <$38.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\n### 5-1 Conviction Score (0-15)\n1. Business quality: **3/5** (narrow moat, FCF strong, generic overhang)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: **1/5** (MoS \u221227%)\n3. Macro alignment: **2/5** (rates high, regime stagflation/reflation)\n4. Thesis clarity: **4/5** (clear KPIs: LUMRYZ TRx, LYBALVI TRx, Ph3 data, debt paydown)\n5. Execution traceability: **4/5** (beat-and-raise 2025-26, buybacks at $28, Avadel integration on track)\n**Total = 14/15 \u2192 Very High business conviction; but Layers 1.5-3 and 5-3 caps apply.**\n\n### 5-2 Conviction Decay\n-1 point every 6 months without confirming evidence. The Q4-2026 ALKS-7290 PoC readout and Q2-2026 REVITALYZ confirmation are the next confirmatory events.\n\n### 5-3 Sizing\n- Actionable conviction at T0 price: **LOW** (valuation override). Maximum starter weight **0-2%**; full position 5% requires \u2264$38.\n- Engine-4 option-content cap applied: pipeline is ~37% of IV \u2192 cap 5% even at fair value.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- **Short in