d in China with positive Phase 3 NT1 results; ALKS's alixorexton will be second to market, if it ever launches \u2014 and the market is valuing it as if it were first.\n4. Adjusted EBITDA margin guidance of 21\u201322% for 2026 (vs 27% in 2025) proves the core is losing operating leverage \u2014 the LUMRYZ launch and R&D ramp are consuming all cash growth.\n5. Short interest at 12.4% suggests informed shorts see the same data; the 16% MoM decline in short interest is just covering into strength.\n6. Royalty streams (J&J INVEGA franchise, VUMERITY) are structurally declining; the data pack shows revenue already down from $1.66B (2023) to $1.48B (2025) before the deal.\n7. Pro-forma net debt + high fixed costs + GAAP losses through 2026 = a balance sheet that is fine only if everything goes right.\n\n**Logic Combat Score: Long (my base) vs Short (my base)** \u2014 Long 4/10 vs Short 6/10 \u2192 Short materially stronger. **Conviction downgraded from Medium (7) to Low-Medium (6).**\n\n**Adversarial data**: no Hindenburg-type report found on ALKS [Unconfirmed], but the 52-filing count and bidding-war disclosures attracted scrutiny. Risk of activist/whistleblower news is unresolved.\n\n**Killed arguments that could revive:**\n- If LUMRYZ achieves >$700M by 2029 AND alixorexton gets 2028 approval, the stock would re-rate to $60+. My base case kills this as low-probability (20%).\n- If the orexin class proves superior to sodium oxybate and Takeda flops commercially, ALKS could still be the best-in-class later entrant \u2014 but being second-to-market with a cheaper class is not my base.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS**\n\n**A. Methodology:** Pass \u2014 Engine selected by data, not by desired output. Blended Engine 3/4 disclosed. Approved.\n**B. Valuation:** Pass \u2014 DCF shown with explicit forecast, WACC derivation, and reverse-DCF. SBC expensed; working capital normalized. Approved.\n**C. Bias:** Fail \u2014 Initial instinct to anchor on sell-side mean target ($56) was rejected by my valuation, but the momentum narrative could still have biased me toward the bull. Correction: I tested the bull scenario at only 20% probability; passed after correction. Approved (with noted correction).\n**D. Consistency:** Pass \u2014 Revenue, margin, SBC, capex paths match the data tags.\n**E. Narrative:** Fail once \u2014 \"long-term potential\" phrase initially drafted; removed. No narrative without number remains. Approved.\n**F. Red Team:** Pass \u2014 Short thesis scored stronger than long thesis. Disclosed.\n**G. Data integrity:** Fail (unresolved) \u2014 (i) $1.32B vs $0.589B cash/investments discrepancy; (ii) institutional ownership 1.1% flagged unreliable; (iii) Beta 0.268 vendor figure untrusted; (iv) Q2 2026 earnings-call Q&A not held. These gaps lower model confidence to **60%**.\n**Final Audit:** Conditional pass after the above corrections.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY**\n\n- Date: 2026-08-24. T0 price: $48.83.\n- IV range: $15\u201358; my base: $31; expected value: $30.7.\n- Key assumptions: LUMRYZ peak $650M; alixorexton 60% success / $550M peak; WACC 8.2%; terminal growth 1.0%.\n- Red team concerns: second-to-market orexin; Takeda class winner; deal overpayment; margin compression.\n- Data unresolved: cash balance and ownership figures.\n- Instruction to future me: re-review **only** when LUMRYZ FY2027 \u2265 $420M or alixorexton Phase 3 NT1 topline positive.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 12 \u2014 FINAL EXECUTION OPINION**\n\n- **Action: Avoid / Reduce if held.**\n- **Conviction: 6/15 (Low-Medium).**\n- **Target weight: 0% for new money; trim existing positions into any strength above $50.**\n- **Strategy: Do not initiate. If an existing position exists, exit 50% immediately; hold the rest only as a small (\u22641%) speculative position until alixorexton Phase 3 readout.**\n- **Entry point for re-initiation (speculative only): $30\u201332**, corresponding to ~1.0\u00d7 sales and my base-case IV.\n- **