ients and +40% YoY [Actual: Q4'25 call]; (2) it is the only\n  once-nightly oxybate, a genuine product-differentiation story; (3) Phase 3 IH\n  (idiopathic hypersomnia) readout was positive [Estimate: FiercePharma / web brief \u2014\n  unverified against filing], creating an sNDA path; (4) integration is a tuck-in of\n  a commercial asset, not an R&D bet. Deviation \u2248 1.5\u00d7 base rate \u2014 acceptable.\n\u2022 alixorexton PoA 55% (base) vs Phase 3 CNS base rate 55\u201365%: No deviation.\n\n\u25a0 Step 1.5-3 Base Rate Shock Check\n\u2022 Success probability (LUMRYZ) >1.5\u00d7 base rate? Yes, but justified above.\n\u2022 alixorexton PoA 55% \u2264 1.0\u00d7 base rate. No red flag.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 Step 2-1 Business Understanding (3 sentences)\nAlkermes is a neuroscience-focused pharmaceutical company selling four proprietary\nproducts: LUMRYZ (once-nightly sodium oxybate for narcolepsy/IH), LYBALVI (oral\nantipsychotic for schizophrenia/bipolar), VIVITROL (long-acting injectable for\nalcohol/opioid dependence), and ARISTADA (long-acting injectable antipsychotic).\nIt also earns manufacturing and royalty revenue on partnered long-acting\nantipsychotics (e.g., J&J) and VUMERITY royalties (Biogen). Its pipeline is built\naround oral orexin-2 receptor agonists (alixorexton in Phase 3 narcolepsy;\nALKS 7290 in ADHD; ALKS 4510 in neurodegenerative fatigue).\nUnderstandability: HIGH.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-2 Moat Assessment + Direction\n\u2022 Intangible assets (brand/specialty relationships): 2/3\n\u2022 Switching costs (physician/patient inertia, LAI depot administration): 2/3\n\u2022 Network effects: 0/3\n\u2022 Cost advantage (proprietary LAI manufacturing): 2/3\n\u2022 Economies of scale: 2/3\n\u2022 Regulatory barriers (LAI generics hard to manufacture): 2/3\n\u2022 Data moat: 0/3\n  Total: 10/21 \u2192 NARROW MOAT.\nMoat direction: VIVITROL NARROWING (generic entry 2027 per mgmt [Actual: Q4'25 call]);\nLUMRYZ WIDENING (only once-nightly, ~40% patient growth); LYBALVI STABLE;\nalixorexton would WIDEN if approved. Net: Stable-to-narrowing over 3 years.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-3 Lynch Classification\nSTALWART with a growth kicker. Core products are steady, cash-generative;\nLUMRYZ is the fast-grower (2025 net sales $279M, +40% [Actual]). Checkpoints:\nstalwart dividend not applicable (no dividend); the thesis depends on product\ncycles, not macro.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-4 Financial Strength Scorecard\n\u2022 Revenue 3-yr CAGR (2022\u21922025): +9.9% [Arithmetic: 1.112\u21921.476]\n\u2022 Revenue latest 4Q (TTM): $1.668B [Actual: 10-Q-derived]\n\u2022 Operating margin FY2025: +17.2% [Arithmetic: 254/1,476]; 12-yr median: \u22129.9% [Data pack]\n\u2022 Adj EBITDA FY2025: $394M [Actual: Q4'25 call]; 2026E guide: $370\u2013410M [Actual]\n\u2022 ROE (TTM): 3.9% [Aggregator \u2014 depressed by acquisition charges]; GAAP ROIC ~10% [Estimate]\n\u2022 FCF FY2025: $0.480B [Actual: filed]; FCF conversion vs OCF: 92% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Net debt at 6/30/26: ~$0.87\u20130.90B [Estimate: 10-Q cash $691.6M, term loan $1.525B less paydown]\n\u2022 Interest coverage (adj EBITDA/interest): 390/80 \u2248 4.9\u00d7 [Estimate]\nJudgment: GOOD (cash-flow strong; leverage moderate; G