ap 5% even at fair value.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- **Short interest**: 12.43% of float; 15.02M shares; 5.71 days to cover; MoM **\u221216.4%** (shorts covering as stock ran +94% off $25.17 low) \u2014 squeeze fuel present on positive pipeline news; but also reflects genuine binary skepticism.\n- **Institutional ownership**: 1.1% [Unconfirmed \u2014 almost certainly an aggregator artifact; treat as unreliable]. Passive-flow tailwind unverifiable.\n- **Insider activity**: 1.41% ownership; no cluster buys/sells retrieved [Unconfirmed]. Company buyback at $28 (not at $49) is the honest insider signal.\n- **Options**: not retrieved [Unconfirmed].\n- **Sentiment**: Sell-side mean $56 / median $58 (stale, 12-day) \u2014 mildly bullish street; stock near $48.83 vs 52-wk high $55.67 \u2014 momentum positive, but crowding moderate.\n- **Crowding Risk Score: 6/15** \u2014 high short interest + bullish consensus = two-sided store of risk. No size reduction needed because we hold 0%.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nALKS is a defensive-growth healthcare name with low historical beta, negative correlation to tech, and a cash-generative core. It fits a barbell (defensive compounders + biotech optionality). Within a diversified book, a 2-3% hold is acceptable; a 0% new position is warranted at T0. **Sector cap: healthcare \u226420%.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\nScenarios (3-yr): \u221255% (25%), +2% (50%), +37% (25%) \u2192 Expected return \u2248 **\u22123%** per 3 years; variance \u2248 0.14.\nKelly fraction = \u03bc / \u03c3\u00b2 \u2248 \u22120.21 \u2192 **Negative. Full Kelly = 0%; fractional (25%) = 0%.**\nVerdict: mathematical position size at T0 is **zero**. The buy-limit discipline respects the Kelly criterion.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n**Risks:**\n1. VIVITROL generic entry 2027 (management openly planning \"multiple scenarios\") \u2014 26% of 2026 revenue at risk.\n2. Alixorexton Phase-3 failure (45% 