al allocation)\n- Short logic strength: 7/10 (valuation + binary risk + base erosion)\n- **Gap = 1 \u2192 Conviction downgraded** \u2713 (consistent with No Position)\n\n### 9-3 Adversarial Data\nNo Hindenburg-style reports retrieved [Unconfirmed]. The 52-filing count in 2026 reflects M&A disclosure, not necessarily malfeasance \u2014 but we note the unknown content of pending proxy/term-loan filings.\n\n### 9-4 Killed Arguments\n- \"The orexin platform is worth $5B because Lilly entered the space\" \u2014 **Killed**: validation \u2260 de-risking; Lilly's entry increases future competition. Active only if Ph3 data is clean and shows clear differentiation.\n- \"LUMRYZ will hit $1B by 2030\" \u2014 **Killed for base case**: Jazz + generics + GTN pressure cap it at $670M. Active only if IH launches early-2028 and narcolepsy TRx compound >25%.\n- \"The $28 buyback proves the stock is cheap at $49\" \u2014 **Killed**: management's own revealed preference says they will not buy at T0 price.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\n**A. Methodology** \u2014 PASS: Blended Engine 3/4; no DCF-only, multiple-only, or TAM-only conclusion.\n**B. Valuation** \u2014 PASS: SBC expensed via GAAP-EBIT bridge; step-up and one-time charges normalized out; alixorexton excluded from core revenue to prevent double-count; 2026 product revenue anchored to company guidance [Actual]; 2027-30 explicitly [Assumption].\n**C. Bias/Overconfidence** \u2014 PASS: alixorexton PoS 55% \u2248 CNS base rate (no >1.5\u00d7 breach). MOMENTUM FLAG: stock +94% off lows; our model, not the price, anchors the conclusion.\n**D. Consistency** \u2014 PASS: T0/T-1 timepoints respected; net debt uses Q1-26 company-reported balance sheet (not stale vendor $70M debt).\n**E. Narrative** \u2014 PASS: \"Orexin platform\" valued as an option with explicit probabilities, not as a base-case earnings stream.\n**F. Red Team** \u2014 PASS: full short thesis + logic combat included; gap \u22642.\n**G. Data Integrity** \u2014