del acquisition (closed 2026-02-12), ALKS owns four proprietary brands: VIVITROL, ARISTADA, LYBALVI (neuropsychiatry/addiction) and LUMRYZ (narcolepsy), plus royalty/mfg streams (VUMERITY; J&J long-acting paliperidone franchise; Otsuka/Lundbeck).\n- T0 price $48.83; market cap $8.192B [Aggregator, 2026-08-24].\n- FY2025 (T-1): Total revenue $1.476B; GAAP NI $0.242B; OCF $0.521B; capex $0.040B; FCF $0.480B; SBC $0.099B [Filed].\n- FY2026 guidance (Tpf): Revenue $1.73\u20131.84B; GAAP net loss ($115)\u2013($135)M; adjusted EBITDA $370\u2013410M; GAAP diluted loss/share ~$0.70; Q2 LUMRYZ guidance raised to ~$350M [Actual \u2014 8-K, 2026-02-25; Q2 call via MarketBeat/Investing.com].\n- Primary discrepancy flag: Data-pack cash+ST investments at FY2025 ($0.389B+$0.200B) totals $0.589B, while company discloses $1.32B cash+investments+restricted cash at 12/31/25 [Actual \u2014 EX-99.1]. This gap is material to net debt. I use the company-filed $1.32B for balance-sheet logic and note the unresolved discrepancy.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 1 \u2014 MACRO CONTEXT**\n\n**1-1 Macro Variables [Actual, retrieved 2026-08]**\n- 10Y UST yield: 4.71% (2026-08-21) [TradingEconomics].\n- Real 10Y (4.71% \u2013 3.4% CPI): ~1.3% positive [Arithmetic].\n- DXY: not anchored in my data; treated as mid-range [Unconfirmed].\n- Fed stance: market perception of Fed reluctance to tighten with above-target inflation (Citadel commentary, 2026-08-17) [Estimate \u2014 secondary source].\n- Inflation: CPI 3.4% in July 2026, down from 3.5% in June [Actual \u2014 TradingEconomics].\n- GDP: Q2 2026 advance +1.5% annualized [Actual \u2014 BEA, 2026-07-30].\n- Credit spreads: not held in data; treated as neutral [Unconfirmed].\n\n**1-2 Regime Probabilities**\n- **Reflation (High rates + growth): 35%** \u2014 growth below trend, inflation above target, rates elevated.\n- **Stagflation (High rates + low growth): 30%** \u2014 1.5% GDP + 3.4% inflation is the closest historical analogue.\n- **Goldilocks (Low rates + growth): 20%** \u2014 inflation still elevated makes this less likely.\n- **Recession (Low rates + low growth): 15%** \u2014 Fed forced into cuts.\nTotal = 100% [Assumption \u2014 based on above data].\n\n**1-3 Macro Sensitivity (each -3 to +3)**\n- Rates: -2 (pipeline value is long-duration; biopharma).\n- Dollar: +1 (minimal ex-US revenue; Ireland domicile but US-centric earnings).\n- Liquidity: 0 (low beta, no commodity linkage).\n- Cycle: +1 (healthcare defensive).\n- Commodities: 0.\nNet sensitivity: moderately rate-negative, otherwise defensive.\n\n**1-4 Macro Alignment**\n- Weighted macro impact: (0.35\u00d7-1)+(0.30\u00d7-2)+(0.20\u00d7+1)+(0.15\u00d7-1) = -0.85 \u2192 mild headwind.\n- Judgment: **Headwind** \u2014 conviction -0.5 steps; no new capital deployment at current price.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN**\n\n**1.5-1 Base Rates**\n- Phase 3 \u2192 FDA approval, CNS drugs with positive class data: ~55\u201365% [Estimate \u2014 historical industry rates].\n- Biotech Phase 3 \u2192 commercial success (peak sales > $500M): ~30\u201340% [Estimate].\n- Large M&A (>$2B) achieving ROIC > WACC over 5 years: ~25\u201335% [Estimate \u2014 framework base rate].\n- 5-year survival of a commercial-stage pharma with 4 marketed drugs: >85% [Estimate].\n- Platform/branded portfolio transition success (neuropsych \u2192 sleep medicine): ~50\u201360% [Estimate].\n\n**1.5-2 Deviation from Base Rate**\n- My base-case DCF implies a ~$31/share fair value, roughly 36% below the market price. This deviates negatively from the market-implied success case. Justifications for my conservatism requiring at least 3 company-specific factors:\n  1. LUMRYZ faces Jazz (Xywav/Xyrem) with entrenched share in a $2.5B narcolepsy market; ALKS must execute a major sales-force buildout while also funding the orexin pipeline.\n  2. Core franchises VIVITROL/ARISTADA are flat-to-declining; J&J long-acting antipsychotic royalty stream faces generic paliperidone pal