ation**\n- **Stalwart-to-Fast-Grower hybrid** \u2014 LUMRYZ growth offsets maturity in legacy brands. Core checkpoints: earnings consistency (poor \u2014 GAAP loss in 2026 from amortization), cash generation (good), competitive durability (moderate).\n\n**2-4 Financial Strength Scorecard [Filed / Arithmetic]**\n- Revenue 3-yr CAGR (2022\u21922025): (1476/1112)^(1/3)-1 = 9.9%. \n- Revenue growth, FY2024\u2192FY2025: -5.2% (decline due to oncology divestiture; continuing ops grew 9% proprietary sales).\n- Operating margin FY2025: 17.2%; 12-yr median: -9.9%.\n- ROE (FY2025): 242/1465 = 16.5%; real GAAP return on tangible assets: healthy.\n- FCF conversion: OCF 0.521B / NI 0.242B = 2.15\u00d7 \u2014 high-quality cash earnings.\n- Net debt pre-Avadel: cash $0.389B + ST inv $0.200B minus LT debt $0 (pack) / company: cash+investments $1.32B; debt ~$0.29B + leases \u2192 net cash ~$1.0B [Estimate].\n- Post-Avadel (pro-forma): net debt ~$745M [Estimate] \u2014 my central case.\n- **Judgment: Good underlying business economics; temporarily distorted 2026 GAAP.**\n\n**2-5 Capital Allocation Scorecard (Total 15)**\n1. Buyback efficiency (net buyback -0.3% FY25; SBC offsets partially): 2/3.\n2. M&A track record (Avadel $2.4B at 8\u00d7 peak sales; execution risk high; prior oncology divestiture): 1/3.\n3. Capex efficiency (light $40M capex; incremental ROIC >20% on low capital): 3/3.\n4. Rationality of mix (R&D ramp + acquisition debt + launch costs): 2/3.\n5. Guidance accuracy (2025 revenues hit; 2026 guidance maintained at Q2; Q2 EPS miss due to deal charges): 2/3.\n- Insider ownership: CEO transition (Pops\u2192Blair) official 2026-09-01; no cluster insider buying in data \u2192 0 bonus.\n**Total: 10/15 \u2014 Good.**\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS**\n\n- R&D capitalization: FY2025 R&D $324M; if capitalized 4-yr amortization, adjusted operating income rises ~$243M (one year) but invested capital also rises. Adjusted NOPAT margin \u2248 20\u201323% vs reported 17.2% [Estimate].\n- SBC treatment: Adjusted FCF = reported FCF - SBC = 480 - 99 = **$381M** (FY2025) [Arithmetic]. My forward valuation uses post-SBC FCFF.\n- Operating lease: only $70M [Filed] \u2014 immaterial to coverage.\n- Brand/data asset estimation: LUMRYZ orphan position and LAI manufacturing know-how arguably add ~$500M to replacement value [Assumption].\n- **Adjusted ROIC** \u2248 20% (with R&D capitalization) vs GAAP ROIC ~10\u201311%; gap driven by expensed R&D and acquisition amortization [Estimate].\n- **Owner Earnings FY2025** = NI $242M + D&A $27M - maintenance capex $30M - \u0394WC ($436M source) \u2248 **$280M normalized** [Arithmetic/Assumption]. The large 2025 WC source is not repeatable; normalized run-rate ~$280\u2013320M [Estimate].\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION ENGINE**\n\n**Engine Selection (Layer 0)**\n- Archetype: **D (Product-Platform Hybrid)** with **E (Option-Led)** transition triggers in the orexin pipeline.\n- Engine: **Blended \u2014 Engine 3 (Hybrid commercial core) \u00d7 70% + Engine 4 (Expectation/Pipeline rNPV) \u00d7 30%**.\n- Rationale: Core revenue is current products (Tier 1); the pipeline is a genuine post-2028 optionality. Using a pure DCF understates optionality; using pure Engine 4 would overstate current cash generation.\n- Transition trigger: If alixorexton reaches Phase 3 success and LUMRYZ \u2265 $500M, reclassify to B (Quality Compounder). Conviction -0.5 step until then.\n\n**Discount-Rate Derivation**\n- Risk-free: 10Y UST 4.71% [Actual].\n- Equity beta: vendor 0.268 flagged unreliable [Aggregator]; fundamental pharma beta ~0.95 [Assumption].\n- ERP: 4.5% [Assumption].\n- Cost of equity: 4.71% + 0.95 \u00d7 4.5% = **9.0%**.\n- Pre-tax cost of debt: term loan ~5.5% [Estimate \u2014 secured term loans due 2031]; tax rate 21% \u2192 **4.3% after-tax**.\n- Weights: E = $8.19B; D = $1.525B + leases $0.07B = $1.595B; D/(D+E) = 16.3%.\n- **WACC = 0.837 \u00d7 9.0% + 0.163 \u00d7 4.3% = 8.2%** [Assumption].\n\n**Core Portfolio FCFF Forecast (post-SBC, unlevered, $M)**\n\n| Year | Revenue | Adj EBITDA % | EBITDA | SBC | Capex | Cash Tax | FCFF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 1,785 | 21.9% | 390 | 110 | 40 | 0 | **290** |\n| 2027 | 1,894 | 25.5% | 483 | 115 | 45 | 15 | **308** |\n| 2028 | 1,964 | 28.0% | 550 | 120 | 50 | 25 | **355** |\n| 2029 | 2,004 | 28.0% | 561 | 120 | 50 | 30 | **361** |\n| 2030 | 2,019 | 29.0% | 585 | 125 | 50 | 35 | **375** |\n| 2031 | 2,014 | 29.0% | 584 | 125 | 50 | 40 | **369** |\n\n- Revenue 2026 from guidance midpoint [Actual]. Revenue 2027\u201331: [Assumption] \u2014 LUMRYZ $350M\u2192$650M peak; LYBALVI $390M\u2192$460M; VIVITROL/ARISTADA/royalties decline at 2\u20135% p.a. This path is NOT guided beyond FY2026; it is my estimate. Sensitivity shown below.\n- EBITDA margins: 2026 guided; 2027+ [Assumption] \u2014 R&D tapers from $465M to ~$400M; SG&A deleverages from LUMRYZ; margin expansion is the key upside risk.\n- SBC/capex: history-anchored [Estimate].\n- Terminal growth: **1.0%** [Assumption \u2014 below nominal GDP].\n- PV of FCFF @8.2%: 268 + 263 + 280 + 263 + 253 + 230 = **$1,557M**.\n- PV of terminal value (369 \u00d7 1.01 / 0.072 = $5,176M; discount 6 yrs): **$3,224M**.\n- **Core EV = $4,781M**.\n\n**Pipeline rNPV (Engine 4)**\n- Alixorexton (NT1): P(approval)=60% [Assumption, anchored by Takeda class success and Phase 2 Vibrance-2 positive results]; launch 2029; peak sales $550M by 2033; after-tax margin 25%; PV @10% risk-adjusted = **$669M**.\n- Alixorexton (NT2/IH): P=35%; peak $300M; launch 2030; PV = **$158M**.\n- ALKS 7290 orexin in ADHD and fatigue pipeline: P=15%; peak $200M; launch 2032; PV = **$40M**.\n- **Total pipeline rNPV = $867M** [Assumption-heavy].\n\n**Enterprise Value & Equity Bridge**\n- Core EV $4.78B + Pipeline $0.87B = **$5.65B EV** [Estimate].\n- Net debt: $1.525B term loans + $0.07B leases - cash/investments post-deal (12/31/25 $1.32B - $775M deal cash + H1 2026 OCF ~$200M) \u2248 **-$0.78B net debt** [Estimate].\n- Equity value = 5.65 - 0.78 = **$4.87B**.\n- Per share (168.7M diluted): **$28.9**.\n\n**Reverse DCF (what market implies)**\nAt $48.83, EV \u2248 $8.19B + $0.78B = $8.97B. With the same pipeline assumption, the core business must be worth $8.1B \u2014 equivalent to FCFF of ~$650M growing at 2% \u2014 or pipeline peak sales must be ~$2.5B with >70% success. Both are excessive relative to my data-based path. **Reverse-DCF judgment: Excessive.**\n\n**Tornado Sensitivity (top 3 variables)**\n1. LUMRYZ peak sales ($400M\u2192$800M) \u2014 swing \u00b1$1.1B EV.\n2. Alixorexton P\u00d7peak ($0.3B\u2192$2.0B) \u2014 swing \u00b1$1.3B EV.\n3. 2028+ adjusted EBITDA margin (24%\u219232%) \u2014 swing \u00b1$0.9B EV.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS**\n\n- Competitive response: If LUMRYZ scales, Jazz has pricing power and an existing sales force; Jazz already counters with patient-access programs. Takeda's oveporexton (approved in China; positive Phase 3 NT1) could redefine narcolepsy treatment paradigms before alixorexton launches \u2192 competitive response risk **-2**.\n- Reflexivity: High price helps recruit, but the current price also enables discounted share issuance for pipeline needs. The company is not cash-hungry today; reflexive risk is low.\n- Customer behavior evolution: LUMRYZ targets the ~50\u201370% of narcolepsy patients failing on first-line therapy; as penetration moves from early adopters to mainstream, payer scrutiny will increase. LTV remains high; churn low due to chronic nature.\n\n---\n\n**SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)**\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Price | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 30% | $18 | LUMRYZ stalls at $400M; alixorexton fails or is significantly delayed; generics crush royalty stream; 2027 GAAP still negative. |\n| Base | 50% | $31 | LUMRYZ reaches $650M; alixorexton approved 2029 with moderate $550M peak; margins expand to 29%. |\n| Bull | 20% | $48\u20135