e rate. Justifications: (1) LUMRYZ already generated $279M FY2025\n  revenue with ~3,500 patients and +40% YoY [Actual: Q4'25 call]; (2) it is the only\n  once-nightly oxybate, a genuine product-differentiation story; (3) Phase 3 IH\n  (idiopathic hypersomnia) readout was positive [Estimate: FiercePharma / web brief \u2014\n  unverified against filing], creating an sNDA path; (4) integration is a tuck-in of\n  a commercial asset, not an R&D bet. Deviation \u2248 1.5\u00d7 base rate \u2014 acceptable.\n\u2022 alixorexton PoA 55% (base) vs Phase 3 CNS base rate 55\u201365%: No deviation.\n\n\u25a0 Step 1.5-3 Base Rate Shock Check\n\u2022 Success probability (LUMRYZ) >1.5\u00d7 base rate? Yes, but justified above.\n\u2022 alixorexton PoA 55% \u2264 1.0\u00d7 base rate. No red flag.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 Step 2-1 Business Understanding (3 sentences)\nAlkermes is a neuroscience-focused pharmaceutical company selling four proprietary\nproducts: LUMRYZ (once-nightly sodium oxybate for narcolepsy/IH), LYBALVI (oral\nantipsychotic for schizophrenia/bipolar), VIVITROL (long-acting injectable for\nalcohol/opioid dependence), and ARISTADA (long-acting injectable antipsychotic).\nIt also earns manufacturing and royalty revenue on partnered long-acting\nantipsychotics (e.g., J&J) and VUMERITY royalties (Biogen). Its pipeline is built\naround oral orexin-2 receptor agonists (alixorexton in Phase 3 narcolepsy;\nALKS 7290 in ADHD; ALKS 4510 in neurodegenerative fatigue).\nUnderstandability: HIGH.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-2 Moat Assessment + Direction\n\u2022 Intangible assets (brand/specialty relationships): 2/3\n\u2022 Switching costs (physician/patient inertia, LAI depot administration): 2/3\n\u2022 Network effects: 0/3\n\u2022 Cost advantage (proprietary LAI manufacturing): 2/3\n\u2022 Economies of scale: 2/3\n\u2022 Regulatory barriers (LAI generics hard to manufacture): 2/3\n\u2022 Data moat: 0/3\n  Total: 10/21 \u2192 NARROW MOAT.\nMoat direction: VIVITROL NARROWING (generic entry 2027 per mgmt [Actual: Q4'25 call]);\nLUMRYZ WIDENING (only once-nightly, ~40% patient growth); LYBALVI STABLE;\nalixorexton would WIDEN if approved. Net: Stable-to-narrowing over 3 years.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-3 Lynch Classification\nSTALWART with a growth kicker. Core products are steady, cash-generative;\nLUMRYZ is the fast-grower (2025 net sales $279M, +40% [Actual]). Checkpoints:\nstalwart dividend not applicable (no dividend); the thesis depends on product\ncycles, not macro.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-4 Financial Strength Scorecard\n\u2022 Revenue 3-yr CAGR (2022\u21922025): +9.9% [Arithmetic: 1.112\u21921.476]\n\u2022 Revenue latest 4Q (TTM): $1.668B [Actual: 10-Q-derived]\n\u2022 Operating margin FY2025: +17.2% [Arithmetic: 254/1,476]; 12-yr median: \u22129.9% [Data pack]\n\u2022 Adj EBITDA FY2025: $394M [Actual: Q4'25 call]; 2026E guide: $370\u2013410M [Actual]\n\u2022 ROE (TTM): 3.9% [Aggregator \u2014 depressed by acquisition charges]; GAAP ROIC ~10% [Estimate]\n\u2022 FCF FY2025: $0.480B [Actual: filed]; FCF conversion vs OCF: 92% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Net debt at 6/30/26: ~$0.87\u20130.90B [Estimate: 10-Q cash $691.6M, term loan $1.525B less paydown]\n\u2022 Interest coverage (adj EBITDA/interest): 390/80 \u2248 4.9\u00d7 [Estimate]\nJudgment: GOOD (cash-flow strong; leverage moderate; GAAP metrics temporarily noisy).\n\n\u25a0 Step 2-5 Capital Allocation Scorecard (total /15)\n1. Buyback efficiency: 1/3 \u2014 shares \u22120.3% 1-yr [Arithmetic]; no significant buyback; SBC offsets.\n2. M&A track record: 2/3 \u2014 Avadel ($2.3B) is a coherent asset, but $26.4M deal costs,\n   $150M inventory step-up, integration risk; record otherwise mixed.\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 \u2014 capex only $40M on $480M FCF; incremental ROIC very high [Estimate].\n4. Rationality of mix: 2/3 \u2014 debt-funded deal (1.525B term loan) but stated paydown intent;\n   R&D reinvestment rational.\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 \u2014 Q2'26 revenue beat ($496M vs $457.4M); 2026 guidance\n   reaffirmed mid-year [Estimate: TipRanks / stockinvest].\nInsider bonus: CEO transition (Pops\u2192Jackson) [Actual: Q2'26 call]; no insider-buy data\n[Unconfirmed] \u2192 0.\nTotal: 11/15 \u2192 GOOD.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 Step 2.5-1 R&D Capitalization\nFY2025 R&D $324M [Actual: Q4'25 call]. Capitalize 50% at 4-yr straight-line \u2192\nadjusted operating income \u2248 $294M vs GAAP $254M (+$40M) [Estimate]. Immaterial to thesis.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2.5-2 SBC Treatment\nFY2025 SBC $99M [Actual: filed]. Adjusted FCF = $480M \u2212 $99M = $381M [Arithmetic].\nThis is the correct owner-oriented FCF; all forward FCFF below deduct SBC.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2.5-3 Operating Lease Capitalization\nFY2025 operating leases $70M [Actual: filed]. Added to net debt: +$70M.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2.5-4 Brand/Data Assets\nSpecialty CNS brands have modest third-party brand value; sales forces are the asset.\nNo numerical adjustment [Assumption].\n\n\u25a0 Step 2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC\nAdjusted NOPAT \u2248 $260M [Estimate] / (Equity $1.82B + lease $0.07B \u2212 cash+investments\n$0.59B per pack, or ~$1.3B per company) \u2192 Adjusted ROIC \u2248 16\u201320% [Estimate].\nNotably above WACC (8.0%). Good.\n\n\u25a0 Step 2.5-6 Owner Earnings (FY2025)\nNet income $242M + D&A $27M \u2212 maintenance capex $40M \u2212 \u0394WC (ex-cash) ~ $20M \u2212 SBC\n$99M [Actual+Estimate] = Owner Earnings \u2248 $110M [Estimate].\nNote: FY2025 OCF ($521M) overstates owner earnings because (a) SBC is added back in\nOCF and (b) working capital built $436M including retained cash.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 Step 0-1/0-2. Archetype: B \u2014 QUALITY COMPOUNDER with an E-type pipeline overlay.\nBlended engine: Engine 1 (DCF + multiples) for the marketed portfolio + explicit\nrNPV option-value module for the orexin pipeline. Rationale (3+ reasons):\n(1) >95% of FY2026E revenue comes from marketed/contracted products;\n(2) the company is FCF-positive and profitable on an adjusted basis (adj EBITDA\n$390M guide), disqualifying pure Option-led treatment;\n(3) but the orexin franchise is worth ~$1.6B at risk-adjusted value [Estimate] \u2014\ntoo large to ignore, so a pure Engine-1 would understate the enterprise.\nTransition status: NOT in archetype transition; core is stable.\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-1 Discount-Rate Derivation (explicit)\n\u2022 Risk-free rate: 4.7% [Actual: FRED DGS10 4.74%, 2026-08-21]\n\u2022 Equity risk premium: 4.75% [Assumption: historical/implied blend]\n\u2022 Beta: 0.80 [Assumption \u2014 fundamental: ungeared ~0.75, relevered at 10% debt weight.\n  The vendor beta of 0.268 is rejected as inconsistent with $1.5B debt and a binary\n  late-stage pipeline; directionally unsupportable. Note IV sensitivity to beta below.]\n\u2022 Cost of equity = 4.7% + 0.80 \u00d7 4.75% = 8.5% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Cost of debt: 7.0% pre-tax [Assumption: SOFR ~4.3% + ~270bps on the 2031 term loan];\n  after-tax at 15% [Assumption] = 5.95% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Weights: E = 8.192/(8.192 + 0.90 + 0.07) = 89.4%; D = 10.6% [Arithmetic, EV \u2248 9.16B]\n\u2022 WACC = 0.894 \u00d7 8.5% + 0.106 \u00d7 5.95% = 8.23% \u2192 USED: 8.0% [Assumption]\n  (rounding down for low effective tax via NOLs and R&D credits).\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-2 Explicit Forecast (2026\u20132030)\n2026 revenue = guidance midpoint $1.785B [Actual: company guidance].\nProduct-level path (2026E \u2192 2030E, $M) \u2014 all [Assumption] unless stated:\n  VIVITROL:      470 \u2192 400 \u2192 300 \u2192 230 \u2192 180   (generic entry 2027 [Actual: mgmt])\n  ARISTADA:      375 \u2192 372 \u2192 365 \u2192 360 \u2192 355\n  LYBALVI:       390 \u2192 430 \u2192 475 \u2192 510 \u2192 540   (TRx +18% Q2'26 [Actual]; decel [Assumption])\n  LUMRYZ:        335 (Alkermes share [Actual: guide]) \u2192 460 \u2192 575 \u2192 700 \u2192 850\n                 (2027 +30%, 2028 +25% incl IH sNDA launch [Assumption])\n  Mfg/royalty:   225 \u2192 140 \u2192 145 \u2192 140 \u2192 135   (Vumerity royalty cliff 2H26 [Actual: guide])\n  alixorexton:     0 \u2192 0 \u2192 0 \u2192 50 \u2192 200         (launch 2029 [Assumption]) \u2014 EXCLUDED\n                 from core DCF to avoid double-count with rNPV; shown for reference.\n  Core revenue total: 1,785 \u2192 1,802 \u2192 1,860 \u2192 1,940 \u2192 2,060 [Arithmetic]\n  (ex-alixorexton).\n\n  FY            2026E    2027E    2028E    2029E    2030E\n  Core revenue   1,785    1,802    1,860    1,940    2,060\n  Adj. EBITDA      390      415      430      455      500   [Assumption: mgmt guide 2026;\n                                       LUMRYZ mix + Vumerity cliff; margins 21.9%\u219224.3%]\n  SBC             (110)    (115)    (115)    (115)    (115)  [Assumption: ~6% of rev; FY25 actual 99]\n  Cash taxes       (10)     (25)     (35)     (50)     (70)  [Assumption: 15% on growing pretax;\n                                       some NOL shelter in 2026\u201327]\n  Capex            (45)     (45)     (45)     (50)     (50)  [Assumption: FY25 actual 40; modest]\n  \u0394WC              (20)     (20)     (15)     (10)     (10)  [Assumption: pack shows high variance]\n  Core FCFF        205      210      220      230      255   [Arithmetic]\n  D&A (incl amort) 125      115      105       95       85   [Assumption: guide 2026 $95\u2013105M\n                                       intangible amort + $27M D&A]\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-3 Terminal Value\nNormalized terminal FCFF = $455M [Assumption: 2030E FCFF 255 + end of heavy\namortization/R&D drag (~$200M normalized add-back) \u2014 a judgment call; flagged].\nTerminal growth g = 2.5% [Assumption: \u2264 long-run nominal GDP].\nTerminal value = 455 / (0.080 \u2212 0.025) = $8,273M [Arithmetic].\nPV of terminal value @8.0% (factor 0.6806) = $5,631M [Arithmetic].\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-4 Core DCF Summary (@8.0% WACC)\nPV of FCFF 2026\u20132030 = 189.8 + 180.0 + 174.6 + 169.1 + 173.6 = $887M [Arithmetic]\nCore enterprise value = 887 + 5,631 = $6,518M [Arithmetic]\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-5 Pipeline Option Value (rNPV module)\n\u2022 alixorexton (NT1/NT2/IH): PoA 55% [Assumption; Phase-3 base rate with BTD];\n  peak sales $1.75B [Assumption]; value at launch = 1,750 \u00d7 2.0\u00d7 EV/S [Assumption]\n  \u00d7 0.55 = $1,925M; discounted 2.5y at 12% risk-adjusted [Assumption] \u2192 PV $1,458M.\n\u2022 ALKS 7290 (ADHD): PoA 12% [Assumption]; peak $1.0B [Assumption]; PV $126M.\n\u2022 ALKS 4510 (fatigue): PoA 8% [Assumption]; peak $0.8B [Assumption]; PV $58M.\nTotal pipeline PV = $1,642M [Arithmetic].\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-6 Enterprise-to-Equity Bridge\nTotal EV = 6,518 + 1,642 = $8,160M [Arithmetic]\nLess net debt: term loan 1,525 [Actual: company release] \u2212 cash+investments 691.6\n[Actual: Q2'26 release] + operating leases 70 [Actual: FY25 filing] = $903M [Arithmetic]\n(CVR liability [Unconfirmed] \u2014 unquantified; conservative direction is additional dilution.)\nEquity value = 8,160 \u2212 903 = $7,257M [Arithmetic]\nPer share (167.76M shares [Actual]) = $43.3 [Arithmetic] \u2014 CENTRAL / BASE CASE.\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-7 Multiples Cross-Check (2026E)\nEV/adj-EBITDA = 9.16 / 0.390 = 23.5\u00d7 [Arithmetic] \u2014 premium to specialty-pharma peer\nmedian (~12\u201316\u00d7 [Assumption]). P/S = 8.19 / 1.785 = 4.6\u00d7 [Arithmetic] \u2014 rich for\nflattish 2027E revenue. Trailing P/E 128.9\u00d7 is noise (acquisition charges). These\nmultiples confirm the market is paying for the pipeline, not the base business.\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-8 Reverse DCF (what price implies)\nAt $48.83 (EV \u2248 $9.16B), after removing pipeline PV ($1.64B), required PV of core\nterminal = $9.16 \u2212 1.64 \u2212 0.887 = $6.63B [Arithmetic] \u2192 required terminal FCF =\n6.63 / 0.6806 \u00d7 0.055 = $536M [Arithmetic]. That implies 2030E core adj EBITDA of\n~$700M [Estimate] vs my base $500M. VERDICT: the market embeds alixorexton success\nAND either LUMRYZ peak >$1B or materially higher margins. FEASIBLE BUT DEMANDING \u2014\nnot an attractive entry.\n\n\u25a0 Step 3-9 Tornado Sensitivity (\u00b11\u03c3)\nTop 3 variables (these are the Thesis KPIs):\n1. alixorexton PoA/peak (IV: 41.1 @35% PoA \u2192 46.6 @70% PoA) [Estimate]\n2. LUMRYZ 2028\u201330 growth (IV: \u00b1$3/share for \u00b110pts CAGR) [Estimate]\n3. WACC / beta (IV: 52.0 @7.0% WACC \u2192 37.6 @9.0% WACC) [Estimate]\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 Step 3.5-1 Competitive Response\n\u2022 If LUMRYZ succeeds, Jazz (Xywav), J&J, and generics will counter with pricing/\n  contracting; IH expansion invites competitors (Xywav already has IH indication).\n  Impact: \u22121 (mild headwind).\n\u2022 If alixorexton succeeds, large CNS players (already active in orexin space) will\n  accelerate competing assets; first-mover advantage is real but time-limited.\n  Impact: \u22121.\n\u2022 VIVITROL generic entry 2027 [Actual: mgmt] \u2192 price erosion scenario already modeled.\n\u25a0 Step 3.5-2 Reflexivity (Soros)\nPositive loop: